WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.300
<i>A kingdom concealed in darkness, Deltora.</i>

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.650
<i>A royal heirloom, the Belt of Deltora.</i>

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.000
<i>Long ago, in this belt fashioned by the first king,</i>

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.750
<i>Seven gems were placed.</i>

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.600
<i>The gems possessed magical powers,</i>

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.350
<i>And were protected while the king's direct descendants wore the belt.</i>

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.150
<i>But, those gems were hidden in seven mystical lands.</i>

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.100
<i>Since then, the kingdom of Deltora has been shrouded in darkness.</i>

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.700
<i>However,</i>

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.200
<i>The light of hope can be seen on the horizon.</i>

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:51.000
<i>Standing against the Shadow Lord, there is a boy who is on a quest to search for the seven gems.</i>

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.000
<i>With light and hope at their side,</i>

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.400
<i>They are off on their adventure.</i>

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:14.170
When I open this door
Kono doa akereba atarashii sekai ga

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.060
A brand new world is beginning
Ima hajimarunda

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.640
Even if there are painful things ahead
Tsurai koto ga aru toshitemo

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:31.040
I will show you that I can overcome them all
Kitto norikoetemiseru

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:38.800
I'm starting to walk in a brand new world now
Atarashii sekai ni ima arukidashita soko ha

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:45.030
And I'm sure there are [Dreams] and [Hope] there
[Yume] ya [Kibou] ga aru kara

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:48.250
This feeling is making my heart beat so fast
Dokidoki suru kono kimochi

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.380
And there's no one who can stop it
Darenimo tomerarenai

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.400
My heart is tightening and out of control
Kyun to hazumu kokoro

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.760
So start flapping your wings from here
Koko kara habataiteiku

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.810
And soar high up into the sky
Ano sora he to takaku

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:09.780
Aiming for [Tomorrow] and [The Future] beyond
[Ashita] [Mirai] mezashite

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.110
We will definitely grow bigger someday
Itsuka ookiku nareru to

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.380
That's what I believed
Sou shinjiteiru no

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:21.540
That's why, just spread your wings
Dakara tsubasa wo hiroge

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:44.800
The Japanese Deltora Quest is brought to you in English by ToranSubs

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.700
<i>Lief and his friends have obtained the two gems, the topaz and ruby</i>

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:56.900
<i>And are on their way to the City of the Rats where the third gem is said to be hidden.</i>

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.800
You're hungry too aren't you Filli?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.700
But we don't have any more food.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.300
Nor very much water.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:09.350
We should go and look for some, but for that we'd need to go through the bushes.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.200
Otherwise we'd be found by the Grey Guards.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.100
Raladin sure was nice...

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.300
We still have five more gems to collect, Lief.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.600
I know that.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.400
We'll just have to push onward, right Filli?

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:38.000
This is still an area Sorceress Thaegan used to control.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.700
Thaegan is gone, but there are her children like Jin and Jod still around.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.100
We need to be careful.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.200
What's that?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.200
Let's go!

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.400
"Tom's Shop. We have everything a traveller needs."?

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.600
There's a shop in this place?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.400
A 'shop'?

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.900
Since you grew up in the forest,
Jasmine, I guess you don't know.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.600
A 'shop' is a place where you buy and sell things.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.300
If we go to the shop, they'll probably sell food there too.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.800
Alright, let's get going.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.700
We're being followed.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.600
And there's a lot of them!

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.700
Are they Grey Guards?

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.500
No. Their footsteps are all over the place.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.600
Also, they're much faster.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.500
The ruby!

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.400
Let's go on ahead, there's nowhere to hide here.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.000
Kree!

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.000
They're still after us!

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.500
They're gaining speed!

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.300
I can sense their bloodthirst back there.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.000
Wolves?

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.500
Then we have to do battle with them,

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.000
before we're attacked!

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.100
Wolves are afraid of fire, so...

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.200
A torch?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.300
Take it.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:28.900
You too, Barda.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.300
And the fire?

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.600
T-Thanks...

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.500
What is this?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.700
"And the names of the children are,

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.400
Hot, Tot, Jin,

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.100
Jod, Fie, Fly,

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:53.500
Zan, Zod, Pik, Snik, Lun, Lod and of course the dreaded Ichabod."

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.700
"And the names of the children are,

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.400
Hot, Tot, Jin,

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.100
Jod, Fie, Fly,

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:09.600
Zan, Zod, Pik, Snik, Lun, Lod and of course the dreaded Ichabod."

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.500
They're not wolves!

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.500
Monsters!

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.400
Our weapons!

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.100
Damn it!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.000
These damn ropes...

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:26.600
That's hot!

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.000
It's them! They're the ones who killed us!

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.300
And they killed Mother as well!

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.600
These fireballs are Jin and Jod.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:39.800
That means... these are Thaegan's thirteen children?!

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.100
More fire, more heat!

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:48.700
Tender, juicy roast meat!

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.200
Watch the fun,

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:56.500
Watch it 'til it's done!

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:01.500
Hear its groans and hear its moans,

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:06.900
Crack and crunch its feeble bones!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.100
More fire!

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.000
More heat!

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.900
Tender, juicy roast meat!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.400
More fire!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.900
More heat!

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:30.400
Tender, juicy roast meat!

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.300
Now we're going to cook and eat you alive!

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.100
You're not getting away.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.650
At this rate, we're really going to be fried for sure!

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.800
Filli!

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.600
Alright! That's good!

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.400
You can cut it!

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.500
Filli...!

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.800
Keep at it!

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.500
They'll realise what we're up to!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:08:01.600
Give me two legs and one head!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.500
What a joke!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.600
Me, Fie

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.400
And me Fly won't accept it!

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:10.800
Give us, Hot and Tot, the same limbs too!

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.600
What's going on?

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.900
They're arguing over which of our body parts each will eat.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.100
I hope they keep fighting,

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.800
That'll buy Filli more time.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.600
Hey, you idiots!!

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:27.700
Lief?!

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.400
Are you saying that you're going to split three among eleven?

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.600
There's no way to do that equally!

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.000
It's impossible!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:41.000
If there's only nine of you, then each of you can get a third, though!

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.900
With nine of us, we'll get a third each!

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:44.700
That's right! Exactly!

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.100
Good! They've started fighting amongst themselves.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.400
Plan success!

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.000
How simple- minded...

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.200
Only nine of us can eat them.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.700
That makes us nine!

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.500
Each will get one third!

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.500
You're right.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.000
But what if there were only three of you?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.000
Between three, each of you can have a whole person to yourself!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:13.700
Stop it!

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.400
Stop that now!

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.500
Alright, now we can buy a little more time.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.300
Stay away!

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.700
Filli, over here!

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:26.900
That's good, Kree!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.500
Now each one of us...

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.900
Can have a whole person!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.600
Now, let's eat.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:42.500
Us and the three of you; we're all different sizes.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.900
Filli, keep at it.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:49.200
If it's one person each, then that's unfair!

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.400
You won't even fill your stomach!

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.600
I want to get full!

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.500
I do too!

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.700
Me too!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.400
You all want to be full,

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.700
But the only way for any of you to be full is if one of you eats all of us!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.000
I want to be full!

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.400
Now's the time, hurry!

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.600
We did it!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.600
You did well, Filli.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.000
Anyway, let's get our weapons back.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.100
They're by the river!

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:40.100
I get to have all three of them to myself!

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:42.800
What d'ya mean, you idiot.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.500
They've escaped!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.900
All while you were arguing!

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.800
There it is; my sword!

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.800
And mine!

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.300
Where's my dagger...?

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.400
There!

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:57.100
The sun is rising!

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.300
They're going to run to the riverside!

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.700
I'm going ahead!

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.100
Wait for me!

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.100
They're coming; not far behind.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:10.000
As if I'm going to let idiots like them catch me!

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.000
The river stops!

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.600
It's a waterfall!

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.400
Are you kidding?!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.800
Is there another way?

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.400
They're here!

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.200
Let's jump!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.400
What?

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:23.700
It's not as far as it looks.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.200
Besides, you don't want to be their breakfast, do you?

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.200
Alright. Let's take them by surprise, then!

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.800
Let's go!

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:43.500
Look! We're out of Thaegan's territory.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.900
Then, what about her children?

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:49.300
Look!

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:50.600
They're not pursuing.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.900
We're saved...

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.600
Far out...

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.900
Hey, look over there!

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.600
Isn't that...

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.700
It's Tom's Shop.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.400
Looks like we made it!

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:08.300
Yeah.

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:30.500
What <i>is</i>  this?

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:34.300
The owner really wants to stand out, doesn't he?

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:45.400
I don't really understand what some of these things are, but they seem interesting.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:52.000
It says: "Free item for every purchase"...

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.500
Let's take a look!

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.700
No one's... here...

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:15.000
"Dear customers, please choose wisely. Absolutely no refunds."

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.600
The owner isn't coming out.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.000
Still, the owner must be very trusting.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.900
Like this, no one would know if we just took something.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:30.900
I can't let go of it!

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:31.900
Barda?

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.300
What are you doing?

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:34.800
I can't let go of it...

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:36.800
Well now,

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:39.100
Has that item taken your interest?

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.000
What's the meaning of this?!

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.500
It just means that Tom isn't so 'trusting', is all.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.500
I'm Tom, the shop owner.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:53.000
Just call me Tom.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:57.100
Now, is there anything you'd like?

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:01.800
For every purchase you'll get something for free.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.000
How about a long, sturdy rope?

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:12.100
This is the best item we have.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:15.700
The price is... three silver coins.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.000
Three silver coins?!

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.200
That's too expensive!

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.900
Dear customer...

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:24.800
You won't find such high quality rope anywhere else!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:44.800
It's magical, is it?

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.200
I'll take it!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.200
Hey!

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.300
That's 'money'?

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:53.200
Yeah, these are silver coins.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.400
It was three, right?

00:14:55.800 --> 00:15:00.200
It seems that the young master has an eye for good value.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:03.800
There are many other wonderful products here too.

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:07.400
'No Bakes', bread you can make just by adding water.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.100
And these are 'Fire Beads'.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:14.200
Wherever they're thrown, a fire will be lit.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:19.400
Well, what else would you like to see?

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:22.000
Please show me everything! All of it!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:24.700
This is amazing too...!

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:28.100
Does it really make a difference
whether or not you have this stuff?

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:32.700
I'm getting the self- coiling rope and the 'No Bakes'!

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:43.400
There are so many other things I want here!

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.100
These are all we can afford.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.000
Out of my way.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.100
How much?

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:14.000
One silver coin, my dear customer.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:16.200
For us it was three...!

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.700
That's a secret sign.

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.300
That's right.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:27.700
It represents the Resistance opposing the Shadow Lord.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.800
Have you heard?

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:36.600
There is a rumour that everything has changed on the other side of the river.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.730
It seems as if Thaegan has died.

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.000
Is that true?

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:46.100
Although, it seems that there are still plenty of thorns growing that way.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:50.700
Thaegan's magic is not the reason why thorns run rampant.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:57.900
It is the result of the King of Deltora turning a blind eye to his people for a century, leaving us scrounging in poverty.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:17:02.300
As such, it is known as 'Del King's Thorns'.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.000
Farewell.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.900
Thank you very much.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.700
Who was that just now?

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.500
Everyone is nameless here.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.300
The only person who has a name is myself.

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:30.200
These are harsh times, so it's better that way.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.400
Jasmine?

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.500
I'll be waiting outside.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:37.500
I have a very good idea of what a 'shop' is now.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:51.200
These here are free of charge.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.500
Why?

00:17:52.500 --> 00:18:00.000
As you can see, it always gives me
great joy to be of help to travellers.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.300
Travellers of justice though, right?

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.400
Thank you very much.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:07.700
And, what's the free item?

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.500
Geez, he's done so much for us already!

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.000
No problem. Here you are.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:16.300
What's... this?

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:17.700
"Water Eaters."

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.030
What's a water eater?

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.300
Jasmine!

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.400
We got a lot of useful things.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.900
Come, let's go to the City of the Rats!

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:38.800
That guy from earlier. If only we had horses too...

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:39.900
I do.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.800
You! Where did you come from?

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:46.400
It's not a horse, but a creature that's very cheap.

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:50.400
Still, were you listening in on all of that?

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.300
I would never miss an opportunity to make a sale.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:59.100
Everything you need can be found at Tom's Shop.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:05.800
These are...?

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.500
Muddlets.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.600
They're so lovely, enjoying their food.

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:12.900
Can they run?

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:17.100
My dear customer, they run like the wind!

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:21.800
They're much sturdier than horses and they listen to you well.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:24.000
When you want them to run, you say "abra",

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.200
And when you want them to stop, you say "katabra".

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.800
We would be able to travel much faster with these guys.

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:33.100
That is true...

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.400
I'll make them cheap.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.600
Say, eighteen gold coins!

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:38.800
That much?!

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:40.300
That's completely unaffordable.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.500
Hold on.

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:48.100
These are 'gold coins', right?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.330
Many thanks!

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.100
Kree,

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:56.600
Filli, we have more comrades now.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.700
Oh, by the way.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:05.400
If you continue down this road, it splits into two directions.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.900
Please make sure that you take the left path.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:11.000
Now, have a safe journey.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:19.200
So when you want to go it's 'abra', and to stop it's 'katabra'.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:22.600
If you had so much money then you should have said so in the first place!

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.900
Still, how did you get all of those gold coins?

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:32.100
When I was living in the forest, I was collecting stuff from the Grey Guards, including those gold coins.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:35.200
Don't you mean 'stealing' rather than 'collecting'?

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.400
They would have stolen the coins from someone themselves.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.900
Just keep quiet. Abra!

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.500
Wait up! Abra!

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:46.100
Abra!

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:02.800
On the right is 'Broad River' and on the left is 'Miller's Rise'...

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:09.100
As I recall, the City of the Rats is a small city just by the Broad River.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.100
What kind of city is it?

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:15.100
It seems that the city is surrounded by walls.

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:19.100
But I've never heard of anyone having entered the city before.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:23.900
So wouldn't that mean that once we go in, we won't get out alive?

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:29.500
Even if that's the case, we have to go there if that's where the gem is!

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:32.900
That right. We have to find the rest.

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:33.000
Fine...
That right. We have to find the rest.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:33.700
Abra!
Fine...

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:34.200
Fine...

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:39.000
Wait! Tom said to go left!

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:44.100
But to get to the City of the Rats, we have to go right.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.300
But...!

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:48.400
Tom doesn't know where we're going.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:51.500
He was just telling us which path was safest and smoothest.

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:52.300
Abra!

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:54.200
A...Abra...

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:03.900
What? What's gotten into them?

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:04.900
Stop! Stop!

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:07.000
There's no use! Stop! Abra!

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:09.400
No, it's katabra!

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:10.400
Katabra!

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:12.800
Katabra!

00:22:12.800 --> 00:22:14.900
Katabra, katabra!

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:17.000
They won't listen! Why?!

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:21.600
Barda!

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:23.200
Jasmine!

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:41.250
Cherry blossom flowers are fluttering down
Sakura maiochite yuku

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:46.920
As if they were peeled from the sky
Sora kara hagareru you ni

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:52.880
I'm gripping and holding hard
Anata to ita omoide ha

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:58.650
The memories I have with you
Zutto gyutto dakishimeteru kara

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:05.950
All of a sudden, flower petals are in full bloom
Futto maue ni ukabu no ha

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:09.550
They're floating right above me
Mankai no hanabira

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:17.330
No matter how long I wait, no one is coming
Mattetatte mou daremo konai

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:24.300
Have I really left my wavering feelings behind?
Yureru omoi ha oitekitandeshou

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:32.540
I'm all alone right here, singing a song about cherry blossoms
Sakura uta utai nagara

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:38.480
Just waiting for no one else but you
Anata wo matsu watashi ha hitori

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:44.490
This love has taught something to me:
Kono koi ga oshiete kureta

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:50.800
That true love is hidden on ordinary days
Heibon na hibi koso ai to

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:59.010
I present my last song to the spring breeze
Harukaze ni saigo no uta wo

00:24:05.900 --> 00:24:08.500
Thaegan's Thirteen Children.

00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:13.700
They're wicked, thieving monsters that assist Thaegan.

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:19.700
They're not as strong as their mother, but they can transform into anything and assault their enemies.

00:24:20.700 --> 00:24:24.000
The perfectly clean city, Noradz.

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:30.300
We were told by the Nine Ra-Kacharz to draw the card of life or death...

00:24:30.300 --> 00:24:30.700
...To make it out alive.

00:24:30.700 --> 00:24:32.400
Clean Noradzeer!

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:34.600
Next time, 'Clean Noradzeer!'.
